{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "units": {
    "length": "m",
    "notes": "Dimensions only; A, I, J and shear areas are computed (FEM::BEAM::computeProperties). IPE / HEA / HEB (h, b, tw, tf, root radius r) and CHS / SHS / RHS (hot finished, outer corner radius 1.5 t, inner 1.0 t): nominal dimensions as given in freely available manufacturer catalogues (e.g. the ArcelorMittal sales programme); the series conform to EN 10365 and EN 10210-2, which are cited for identification only, nothing is copied from the standard documents. RHS height is the longer side (local y). Tube, Rect / Bar, Box and Spar I are representative sizes chosen for this project, not taken from a standard or a catalogue. Tube: thin round tubes in inch sizes (aircraft, vehicle, bicycle) and large rolled tubes (towers). Rect / Bar: solid rectangles (timber, glulam, flat bars) and round bars. Box: light rectangular tubes (outer radius 2 t, inner 1 t). Spar I: extruded wing spar sections (root radius 3 mm). Channels, angles and tees are not in the catalogue: the beam element needs doubly symmetric sections."
  },
